Implemented Vercel Web Analytics for the WDC Learning Portal

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics following the official Vercel documentation (https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart).

## Changes Made:

### 1. Installed @vercel/analytics package
- Added @vercel/analytics@^2.0.1 to package.json dependencies
- Updated package-lock.json with the new package and its dependencies

### 2. Integrated Analytics Component
- Modified client/src/App.jsx:
  - Added import: `import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/react';`
  - Added `<Analytics />` component to the App component within the AuthProvider wrapper
  - This ensures analytics tracking is active across all authenticated and unauthenticated routes

### 3. Verified Implementation
- Build completed successfully with no errors
- All changes preserve existing code structure and functionality
- The Analytics component is properly positioned at the root level to track all page views

## Framework Details:
This is a React + Vite project, so the implementation followed the React/Create React App instructions from the Vercel documentation.

## Next Steps for Deployment:
1. Push these changes to the repository
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard (Analytics → Enable)
3. Deploy the application to Vercel
4. Analytics will start tracking page views automatically after deployment
5. Monitor analytics data in the Vercel dashboard after traffic accumulates

## Notes:
- The Analytics component is lightweight and won't impact application performance
- It tracks page views automatically without requiring additional configuration
- No environment variables or additional setup is needed for basic analytics functionality
- The component works in both development and production environments
